{"$schema":"motion-spec v2 (this folder: MOTION_SPEC.md)","convention":{"rig":"VRM 1.0 normalized humanoid bones (three-vrm getNormalizedBoneNode). VRM 0.x models: apply VRMUtils.rotateVRM0, then negate the X and Z of every rotation and of hipsOffset, because their normalized bones keep the model frame that faces -Z (three-vrm createVRMAnimationClip does the same). Verified by rendering Sendagaya_Shibu in spec poses (artifacts/vrm_poses.png). Gaze sign on VRM 0.x is not verified.","axes":"+Y up, +Z the way she faces, +X her left. Camera on +Z looking at -Z, turned camera.yawDeg around Y (orthographic).","euler":"degrees, order XYZ as three.js Euler (matrix = Rx*Ry*Rz), in the normalized local space, relative to the T-pose (identity). lowerArm is a hinge: only its Y channel moves (X and Z stay 0 +/- 5). That holds because the parent X axis of the forearm is the humerus. upperArm.x is NOT humeral rotation: Rx is the outermost turn about the parent (shoulder) X axis, which is the humerus only in the T-pose, so on a lowered arm it swings the arm. Humeral and femoral rotation are measured by swing-twist decomposition against the limb hanging straight down (check_spec twist rule, lib/limits.mjs TWIST). Forearm pronation and supination are hand.x.","composition":"final local euler = rest + sum(idle layers * idleWeight(t)) + action delta, per channel. idleWeight ramps over idle.rampMs at rest ends (lib/compose.mjs).","signs":{"headX":"+ chin down","headY":"+ turn to her left","headZ":"+ tilt to her right shoulder","leftUpperArmZ":"- lowers the arm","rightUpperArmZ":"+ lowers the arm","leftLowerArmY":"- bends the elbow (forearm forward)","rightLowerArmY":"+ bends the elbow","upperLegX":"- swings the thigh forward","footY":"- turns the right toes out, + the left toes out","upperLegZ":"+ moves the right foot toward her left (adduction of the right leg)","lowerLegX":"+ bends the knee","footX":"+ points the toes"},"curves":"Each track is a list of keys [tMs, value, flags?]; monotone cubic Hermite (Fritsch-Carlson) per channel; tangent 0 at the first and last key and at keys flagged \"h\". Before the first key the first value holds; after the last, the last value.","fingers":"[curl, spread, thumbCurl] deltas added to rest.fingers; a rig maps curl c to each finger joint X = c * [55, 75, 45] deg (proximal, intermediate, distal), spread s to proximal Z = s * [-8,-3,3,8] across index..little, thumb t to thumb joints = t * [20, 35, 40].","gaze":"[yawDeg, pitchDeg] relative to straight ahead of the head; +yaw her left, +pitch up. VRM: lookAt.yaw/pitch (or a lookAt target placed on that ray). 2D: shift the iris layer.","expressions":"VRM 1.0 preset names (happy, relaxed, surprised, aa, ih, ou, ee, oh, blink). Values are deltas added to rest.expressions, clamped to 0..1.","hipsOffset":"metres, added to the hips position (dip, lift).","twoD":"Layered 2D rig (lib/layer2d.mjs): run FK, project with camera.yawDeg. Each limb drawing is pinned at its projected joint, rotated to the projected bone angle, and stretched along the bone by ratio / variant.nominal, where ratio = projected length / true length; the variant is picked from twoD.parts[p].variants by ratio and depth (toward or away from the camera). Head, torso and pelvis pick a turn view by camera-relative yaw and pitch and shift their face parts by parallax between views. Draw order: sort parts by camera depth of their midpoints every frame."},"camera":{"yawDeg":14},"skeleton":{"note":"Proportions used by the checker and preview (1.60 m). A real rig keeps the angles and re-solves the contacts in rest.contacts with its own IK.","bones":{"hips":[null,[0,0.92,0]],"spine":["hips",[0,0.08,0]],"chest":["spine",[0,0.12,0]],"upperChest":["chest",[0,0.12,0]],"neck":["upperChest",[0,0.12,0]],"head":["neck",[0,0.08,0]],"headTop":["head",[0,0.2,0]],"leftShoulder":["upperChest",[0.03,0.06,0]],"leftUpperArm":["leftShoulder",[0.14,0,0]],"leftLowerArm":["leftUpperArm",[0.28,0,0]],"leftHand":["leftLowerArm",[0.23